# Module AIRULES (LAW)

Canonical: `AIRULES/00-AGENT-CONTRACT.md` §2n.

Project `AIRULES/` is the framework contract. A host that packs extend (Shop + payments, public site + templates) **MUST** ship its own handbook so a pack does not invent routes the host never listens to.

## MUST

- Hosts / extendable modules keep **`app/modules/<ThisModule>/AIRULES/`** (English; index + topic files).
- When the user names a host **and** that folder exists: read it **first**, then follow **project AIRULES + those files together**.
- A new host that others will extend **MUST** create this folder in the same work.

## MUST NOT

- Skip a present host `AIRULES/` and register public routes the host does not wake.
- Treat module rules as a replacement for project AIRULES (CRC, PHP 7.4+, finish gate still apply). Conflict → project wins.
- Put host-only law only under project `AIRULES/` (the host zip/folder must carry its handbook).
- Invent a law only under `.cursor/rules/`.

Finish gate: named host + unread `AIRULES/` = fail.
